invariant: INV-60
file: src/mldsa_sign_steps.c
catches: test/ct-taint.sh
reason: a host object's mlds_expand returns at the first polynomial of
  s1 out of range, so its time tells which polynomial failed. The return
  branches on a verdict that a secret decides, before the caller
  declassifies the combined answer (docs/decisions.md 191). Memcheck
  reports the jump in the ML-DSA-87 case of every value.

--- old
        ok &= mlds_unpack_eta(&ex->key.s1_hat[j], sk + MLDS_SK_S1_AT + (size_t)j * MLDS_ETA_BYTES);
--- new
        if (!mlds_unpack_eta(&ex->key.s1_hat[j], sk + MLDS_SK_S1_AT + (size_t)j * MLDS_ETA_BYTES)) {
            return 0;
        }
